            },
            {
              "text": "Old Brown was a quiet bird who did not like noise or bad behavior.",
              "audioStart": 112.612,
              "audioEnd": 116.225
            },
            {
              "text": "Nutkin ran straight to the tree where Old Brown lived and began to bother him without fear.",
              "audioStart": 117.088,
              "audioEnd": 121.688
            },
            {
              "text": "Nutkin brought little gifts like food items and small pieces of wood to Old Brown each day.",
              "audioStart": 122.55,
              "audioEnd": 127.138
            },
            {
              "text": "Every time he gave a gift, he asked the old bird a silly question.",
              "audioStart": 128,
              "audioEnd": 131.637
            },
            {
              "text": "Old Brown sat quietly in his house and never answered any of the questions.",
              "audioStart": 132.5,
              "audioEnd": 136.65
            },
            {
              "text": "Nutkin danced around the tree and laughed because he thought the old bird was too slow.",
              "audioStart": 137.512,
              "audioEnd": 141.762
            },
            {
              "text": "Small boats were used by the group to cross the river.",
              "audioStart": 142.625,
              "audioEnd": 145.312
            },
            {
              "text": "Food that was needed for the winter was collected by the busy animals on the island.",
              "audioStart": 146.175,
              "audioEnd": 150.113
            },
            {
              "text": "The group spent many hours working while Nutkin played around the trees.",
              "audioStart": 150.975,
              "audioEnd": 154.588
            },
            {
              "text": "Nothing could stop the little animal from making noise all day long.",
              "audioStart": 155.45,
              "audioEnd": 158.925
            },
            {
              "text": "The other animals watched him with deep concern as the days passed quickly.",
              "audioStart": 159.787,
              "audioEnd": 163.575
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "Day after day, Nutkin continued this game and became even more confident.",
              "audioStart": 164.438,
              "audioEnd": 168.5
            },
            {
              "text": "He played too close to Old Brown and said things that were quite bad.",
              "audioStart": 169.363,
              "audioEnd": 172.7
            },
            {
              "text": "The other animals watched him with worry because they knew that danger was near.",
              "audioStart": 173.562,
              "audioEnd": 177.188
            },
            {
              "text": "Old Brown remained calm while the little animal made fun of him.",
              "audioStart": 178.05,
              "audioEnd": 181.088
            },
            {
              "text": "Many days passed like this while the visitors collected food on the island.",
              "audioStart": 181.95,
              "audioEnd": 185.613
            },
            {
              "text": "Nutkin thought that Old Brown would never do anything to stop him.",
              "audioStart": 186.475,
              "audioEnd": 189.675
            },
            {
              "text": "He spent his hours jumping around and shouting without any care in the world.",
              "audioStart": 190.537,
              "audioEnd": 194.25
            },
            {
              "text": "The other animals often talked about how dangerous Nutkin's actions really were.",
              "audioStart": 195.113,
              "audioEnd": 199.2
            },
            {
              "text": "They hoped that nothing terrible would happen before the end of their visit.",
              "audioStart": 200.062,
              "audioEnd": 203.525
            },
            {
              "text": "Every warning was ignored by the silly animal who only cared about his own fun.",
              "audioStart": 204.387,
              "audioEnd": 208.463
            },
            {
              "text": "If Old Brown had wanted to attack, he could have caught the silly animal much earlier.",
              "audioStart": 209.325,
              "audioEnd": 213.662
            },
            {
              "text": "The words that were spoken by Nutkin were not nice at all.",
              "audioStart": 214.525,
              "audioEnd": 217.475
            },
            {
              "text": "Everyone watched while the little animal continued his silly games every single afternoon.",
              "audioStart": 218.338,
              "audioEnd": 222.925
            },
            {
              "text": "The visitors often wondered how long Old Brown could stay calm.",
              "audioStart": 223.787,
              "audioEnd": 227.012
            },
            {
              "text": "They knew that every action had a result and that trouble would come soon.",
              "audioStart": 227.875,
              "audioEnd": 231.325
            },
            {
              "text": "Still, Nutkin did not care about any of their warnings or advice.",
              "audioStart": 232.188,
              "audioEnd": 235.912
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "Finally, on the last day of their visit, Nutkin went too far.",
              "audioStart": 236.775,
              "audioEnd": 240.55
            },
            {
              "text": "He sat right on top of Old Brown's chair and pulled the old bird's tail.",
              "audioStart": 241.412,
              "audioEnd": 244.988
            },
            {
              "text": "That action made Old Brown very angry, and he caught the little animal fast.",
              "audioStart": 245.85,
              "audioEnd": 250.062
            },
            {
              "text": "Nutkin tried to run away, but the strong bird held him tight.",
              "audioStart": 250.925,
              "audioEnd": 255.56
            },
            {
              "text": "Old Brown did not hurt him, but he taught the proud animal a hard lesson.",
              "audioStart": 256.423,
              "audioEnd": 260.173
            },
            {
              "text": "After a long struggle, Nutkin broke free and ran away as fast as he could.",
              "audioStart": 261.036,
              "audioEnd": 265.298
            },
            {
              "text": "He lost his beautiful tail during the escape, which made him very sad and quiet.",
              "audioStart": 266.161,
              "audioEnd": 270.56
            },
            {
              "text": "From that day on, Nutkin never bothered anyone again and learned to show proper respect.",
              "audioStart": 271.423,
              "audioEnd": 276.223
            },
            {
              "text": "The other animals were surprised to see how much Nutkin had changed.",
              "audioStart": 277.086,
              "audioEnd": 280.598
            },
            {
              "text": "He returned home safely and spent the rest of his days being good to everyone.",
              "audioStart": 281.461,
              "audioEnd": 285.373
            },
            {
              "text": "His tail was lost while he was trying to run away from the big bird.",
              "audioStart": 286.236,
              "audioEnd": 289.611
            },
            {
              "text": "The lesson that was taught by Old Brown was never forgotten by the young animal.",
              "audioStart": 290.473,
              "audioEnd": 294.173
            },
            {
              "text": "If he had known the danger, he would have behaved much better during the trip.",
              "audioStart": 295.036,
              "audioEnd": 298.673
            },
            {
              "text": "The journey back across the water was quiet and peaceful for all the animals.",
              "audioStart": 299.536,
              "audioEnd": 303.336
            },
            {
              "text": "Nutkin sat alone in his boat and thought about everything that had happened.",
              "audioStart": 304.198,
              "audioEnd": 307.698
            },
            {
              "text": "He finally understood that bad behavior always brings serious results in the end.",
              "audioStart": 308.56,
              "audioEnd": 312.911
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
